# Python pytest cache (the GDScript-via-pytest CI tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# FEAT-292 (resolves PR-001/PR-002): sim_results.json is a GENERATED
# artifact — tests/sim/test_balance_sim.gd (core/sim/simulator.gd's N=1000
# balance regression) rewrites res://sim_results.json on every single test
# run, and two of its seven keys (commit_hash, timestamp) change on every
# regen even when nothing balance-relevant moved. It used to be committed
# to git, which meant `scripts/test_command.sh` (and its N=1000 stage
# specifically) left the working tree dirty after every run — a
# CLAUDE.md commit-hygiene / deployment-gate violation, since nobody was
# ever meant to hand-commit a fresh commit_hash/timestamp pair every time
# the suite executes.
#
# The file stays at its existing res://sim_results.json (repo root) path —
# scripts/ci/check_sim_results_provenance.py, tests/pytest/
# test_sim_results_provenance.py, and .github/workflows/test.yml's
# artifact-upload step all read/write it there — but it is no longer
# tracked by git. Anchored to the repo root (leading `/`) and matched by
# exact filename only, so this rule can never shadow any data/*.tres
# resource file (per CLAUDE.md, data/ files must remain trackable/
# committed) — see tests/ci/test_sim_results_gitignore_feat292.py.
/sim_results.json
